    "## 1. First Look"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6b8676ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Data Shape\n",
    "\n",
    "**Prediction:** Expecting large dataset with significant breadth and volume "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a71c1ef6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df.shape"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f475bd19",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Obvervation:** 300k+ Rows and 122 Columns. \n",
    "\n",
    "**Decision:** Will need to split into statistical categories and potentially similar buckets (i.e. applicant data, security data, social data) for further assessment as attempting look at this number of columns as a whole group will make it difficult to draw tangible conclusions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cc02545c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Class Imbalance\n",
    "\n",
    "**Prediction:** Typically defaulters are a very small percentage of a mortgage loan book as the financial health of bank is reliant on this percentage staying low given the huge losses taken upon mortgage default."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ead79a10",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Percentage distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "df[\"TARGET\"].value_counts(normalize=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Raw value counts\n",
    "\n",
    "df['TARGET'].value_counts(dropna=False) "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5fb2a3a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Observation:** 92% Non Defaulters vs 8% Defaulters\n",
    "\n",
    "**Decision:** Non-Defaulters make up a large portion of the loan book as expected, however 8% default rate is quite high and there may be addressable segements of applicants that are the drivers of this default rate. Indicates the lender has already priced in a riskier target market through rates/fees or is in a vulnerable financial position if the default is not addressed meaningfully through either policy changes or financial controls.\n",
    "\n",
    "No resampling will occur as this is purely a screening exercise, not model training. WOE/IV are computed on the full dsitribution, so class imbalance is a contraint to respect."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6621311f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
