  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f0f8527d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. WOE/IV Computation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "17cd6b23",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Purpose.** Turn the binning decisions from Section 3 into two things: a ranked view of *which* features drive default (**Information Value**), and model-ready **Weight of Evidence** encodings of those features. IV answers \"how predictive?\"; WOE is the monotonic re-expression a scorecard/logit consumes.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Approach.** Hand-roll the WOE/IV mechanic first so the numbers aren't a black box, then optionally cross-check with `optbinning`. Bins and WOE values are derived on the **training split only** and applied to validation/test — fitting on the full data leaks the target.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Leakage guards.**\n",
    "- Exclude id columns (`SK_ID_CURR`) before ranking — a unique key yields spurious near-infinite IV.\n",
    "- Carry the Section 3 Decisions (transforms, missing-as-its-own-bin) into the binning here rather than re-deciding.\n",
    "\n",
    "Rhythm: **Predict → Task → Decision**, each Decision pointing forward to preprocessing/modelling."
