    "### 4.6 Cross-check with `optbinning` _(optional)_"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d99bcdea",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Once the manual version is trusted, `OptimalBinning` gives monotonic/optimal bins plus IV out of the box and a sklearn `fit`/`transform` API. Use it to validate the hand-rolled IVs land in the same ballpark, not to replace the understanding.\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "from optbinning import OptimalBinning\n",
    "ob = OptimalBinning(name=col, dtype='numerical')\n",
    "ob.fit(X_train[col].values, y_train.values)   # train only\n",
    "ob.binning_table.build()                       # WOE + IV table\n",
    "```"
   ]
